/E (AFTER COMPLETING THE RHINO MODEL, I PREPARED THE SEPARATE COMPONENTS FOR 3D PRINTING. THE MAIN BODY AND LID WERE DESIGNED TO FIT TOGETHER WHILE MAINTAINING THE OVERALL SHAPE AND PROPORTIONS OF THE CONCEPT. I USED 3D PRINTING TO BRING THE DIGITAL MODEL INTO A PHYSICAL FORM AND EVALUATE ITS STRUCTURE, SURFACE DETAILS, AND ASSEMBLY. THIS PROCESS HELPED ME UNDERSTAND HOW THE DIFFERENT COMPONENTS CONNECT AND IDENTIFY AREAS WHERE ADJUSTMENTS COULD IMPROVE THE FINAL PRODUCT. IT ALSO ALLOWED ME TO EXPERIENCE HOW A DIGITAL DESIGN TRANSLATES INTO A PHYSICAL OBJECT.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
