<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 238 0 R
/E (I USED GRASSHOPPER IN RHINO TO CREATE A PARAMETRIC CYLINDRICAL FORM. I STARTED BY GENERATING POINTS AND CURVES, THEN USED MATHEMATICAL FUNCTIONS SUCH AS SINE AND COSINE TO CONTROL THE SHAPE AND CREATE AN HOURGLASS-LIKE STRUCTURE. USING COMPONENTS LIKE LOFT, DIVIDE, AND GRAPH MAPPER, I DEVELOPED THE OVERALL FORM AND CONTROLLED ITS VARIATIONS. I THEN CREATED A REPEATED PATTERN OF SMALL RECTANGULAR ELEMENTS AROUND THE SURFACE, USING ROTATION AND MOVEMENT TO GIVE THE MODEL ITS LAYERED, TEXTURED APPEARANCE.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
